The primary deliverable is a discrete categorical raster where each pixel is assigned the unique identifier (GID) corresponding to its classified IUCN GET Ecosystem Functional Group.

@section(Confidence and Purity Metrics)
Alongside the categorical map, the external pipeline generates secondary rasters:
1. *Confidence Map*: Displays the normalized probability score for the assigned EFG, reflecting the trust in the discrimination of classes.
2. *Gini Purity Map:* Provides a metric of class purity, distinguishing pixels with high-confidence class discriminations (up to a value of 1) from pixels with a high probability of class confusions (down to a value of 0).

